  <ferc:FileNameOfSystemMap id="Tag898" contextRef="C251">Great Basin Gas Transmission Company System Map.pdf</ferc:FileNameOfSystemMap>
  <ferc:GeneralInformationOnPlantAndOperationsTextblock id="Tag899" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p class="MsoListParagraph" style="margin-left: .75in; mso-add-space: auto; text-align: justify; text-justify: inter-ideograph; text-indent: -.5in; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1;"&gt;&lt;!-- [if !supportLists]--&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 16.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial;"&gt;&lt;font style="mso-list: Ignore;"&gt;1.&lt;font style="font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 16.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"&gt;Great Basin operates an interstate transmission system extending from the Idaho-Nevada border to the Nevada-California border. The pipeline serves the Lake Tahoe, Reno, Sparks, and Carson City areas and other communities in northern and western Nevada. The FERC regulates the northern Nevada transmission facilities of Great Basin and the rates charged by Great Basin for the transportation of gas for its firm shippers, including Sierra Pacific Power Company (dba NV Energy) and SWG. The Great Basin system includes an LNG peak-shaving facility, which is used to provide third-party gas storage and vaporization services on a contract basis.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: .75in; text-align: justify; text-justify: inter-ideograph; text-indent: -.5in;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 16.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"&gt;2&amp;amp;3. Total plant investment is represented by a pipeline system and related facilities, consisting principally of 899 miles of transmission pipeline and six compressor stations, with a combined rating of approximately 20,500 horsepower. Total utility&amp;#160;plant at December 31, 2025 was approximately $401 million, including construction work in progress. &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:GeneralInformationOnPlantAndOperationsTextblock>
  <ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock id="Tag900" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: .25in; tab-stops: .25in .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 6.5in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 16.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"&gt;1. None&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: .25in; tab-stops: .25in .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 6.5in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 16.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"&gt;2. None&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: .25in; tab-stops: .25in .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 6.5in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 16.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"&gt;3. None&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: .25in; tab-stops: .25in .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 6.5in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 16.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"&gt;4. None&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: .25in; tab-stops: .25in .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 6.5in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 16.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"&gt;5. None&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: .25in; tab-stops: .25in .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 6.5in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 16.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"&gt;6. None&lt;font style="mso-spacerun: yes;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: .25in; tab-stops: .25in .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 6.5in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 16.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"&gt;7. None&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: .25in; tab-stops: .25in .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 6.5in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 16.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"&gt;8. None&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: .25in; tab-stops: .25in .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 6.5in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 16.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"&gt;9. None&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: .25in; tab-stops: .25in .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 6.5in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 16.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"&gt;10. None&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: .25in; tab-stops: .25in .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 6.5in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt; text-indent: -0.25in;"&gt;11. The Company filed a notice of rate change on March 6, 2024.&amp;#160; Motion rates with an overall rate increase of approximately $13 million, subject to refund, became effective September 2024.&amp;#160; Interim Settlement Rates became effective on November 1, 2024.&amp;#160; On December 24, 2024, the Company filed an uncontested offer of settlement.&amp;#160; The offer of settlement is a black box settlement with a pre-tax rate of return of 9.76% and a calculated overall rate increase of approximately $9.6 million.&amp;#160; On March 3, 2025, the Commission issued Letter Order approving the uncontested settlement, which became effective April 2, 2025.&amp;#160; A portion of the rates implemented subject to refund, ($586.5 thousand) reserved pending final outcome in the case, was refunded to Shippers on May 13, 2025.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: .25in;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 16.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"&gt;12.&amp;#160;Effective December 1, 2025, Robert J. Stefani, the Senior Vice President/Chief Financial Officer of Great Basin resigned and Justin S. Forsberg assumed the position.&amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;As of March 17, 2026, Fabio Pineda assumed the role of Vice President/Controller and Chief Accounting Officer of Great Basin.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: .25in; tab-stops: .25in .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 6.5in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 16.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"&gt;13. None&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock>
