&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div class="Section_1"&gt;
&lt;h1 style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: -18pt; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 10pt; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'upperLetter'; -aw-list-number-values: '1'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 26pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;A&lt;/font&gt;.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 26pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;font style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;Notes to Financial Statements&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-weight: normal; font-style: italic; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;Note 1: General&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;Great Basin Gas Transmission Company (Great Basin), a wholly owned subsidiary of Southwest Gas Corporation (SWG), is a natural gas transmission company subject to the jurisdiction of the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (FERC). Accounting records are maintained in accordance with the FERC Uniform System of Accounts (USofA). Great Basin operates a transmission system extending from the Idaho-Nevada border to the Reno, Sparks, and Carson City areas and communities in northern and western Nevada. Great Basin provides transportation services to Sierra Pacific Power Company (dba NV Energy) in Reno and Sparks, Nevada, and to SWG in both North and South Lake Tahoe, California, and in various locations throughout northern Nevada. SWG is a wholly owned subsidiary of Southwest Gas Holdings, Inc. In addition, transportation service is provided through firm and interruptible contracts and capacity release to several large commercial and industrial customers in northern Nevada. The Great Basin system includes an LNG facility, which is used to provide third-party gas storage services on a contract basis.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;Related Party Transactions&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;As noted above, Great Basin provides transmission service on both a firm and interruptible basis, as well as LNG storage service, for its shippers, including its parent company, SWG. Amounts receivable for services to SWG ($34,907,164 billed in 2025) are recorded in FERC account 146, Accounts Receivable from Associated Companies. See also Note 5. &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;Some expenditures related to Great Basin, such as certain construction expenditures and labor-related costs are paid by SWG for the benefit of Great Basin. Amounts payable to SWG are recorded via intercompany accounts payable. See also Note 6. &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;Financing for Great Basin is provided by internally generated cash and as necessary, SWG. Notes payable - parent company represents the debt portion of the SWG investment in Great Basin. This note accrues interest at the rate per annum which is equal to the Great Basin FERC approved cost of debt. The current annual rate is 4.39%. The equity portion of the SWG investment is represented by common stock and retained earnings.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: -36pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 10pt; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'upperLetter'; -aw-list-number-values: '2'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 8pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;B.&lt;font style="width: 8pt; font-variant: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-weight: normal; font-stretch: normal; line-height: normal; display: inline-block;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;Notes to Comparative Balance Sheet and Statement of Income&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4 style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-weight: normal; font-style: italic; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;Note 2: Summary of Accounting Policies, Basis of Reporting, and Updates&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;Gas Utility Plant is stated at cost, less contributions in aid of construction which are netted against Gas Plant. Original cost includes contracted services, material, payroll, and related costs such as taxes and benefits, general and administrative overheads, and an allowance for funds used during construction (AFUDC). The AFUDC rate includes both a debt and equity component (where relevant). Depreciation and amortization are computed utilizing the straight-line remaining-life method at rates considered sufficient to amortize costs over estimated service lives.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;Non-Cash Investing Activities&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;Investing activities in the Statement of Cash Flows have been adjusted for non-cash transactions. Construction expenditures that were not yet paid, thereby remaining in accounts payable, of approximately $1.9 million as of December 31, 2025.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;Gas inventories - The gas stored balance of $267,550, reflected on the balance sheet, represents LNG cushion gas owned by Great Basin and is valued under the average cost method. Great Basin&amp;#8217;s LNG storage facilities include 1,001,835&amp;#160;MMBtu of liquefied natural gas as of December 31, 2025, held on behalf of its customers (including cushion gas).&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;Income Taxes - Deferred tax assets and liabilities are recognized for the future tax consequences attributable to differences between the financial statement carrying amounts of existing assets and liabilities and their respective tax bases. Deferred tax assets and liabilities are measured using enacted tax rates expected to apply to taxable income in the years in which those temporary differences are expected to be recovered or settled.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;Basis of Reporting&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;The financial statements are presented in accordance with the reporting requirements of the FERC. This is a comprehensive basis of accounting substantially consistent with GAAP. Some variability occurs due to reporting requirements of the FERC form that distinguishes line items by the FERC&amp;#8217;s USofA rather than significant functional category under U.S. GAAP. For instance, accumulated deferred taxes in the Balance Sheets, included herein, are reported based upon asset and liability components under the USofA. Similarly, in the Statement of Income, income tax expense has been distinguished between taxes associated with operating income versus other income and deductions in accordance with FERC reporting based on the USofA.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;In areas where options are provided for in accounting orders issued by the FERC, or where related guidance is not prescriptive, and U.S. GAAP is more prescriptive, impacts under U.S. GAAP will typically be reflected in financial line items in FERC reporting.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;SWG administers pension and other benefit plans such that when SWG employees work on Great Basin-related construction projects, their labor and overhead costs (including benefit costs) are applied to Great Basin work orders. Great Basin capitalizes eligible benefit costs when SWG employees work on Great Basin-related construction projects.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;Revenues&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;As indicated in Note 1, Great Basin is subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the FERC, including the rates it can charge its shippers. Its shippers are billed, and revenue is recognized, based upon transmission service utilized and storage activity each calendar month, including certain fixed reservation charges.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;Intangible Assets&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;Intangible assets include franchises and software-related intangibles. The Intangibles balances below are as of December 31, 2025 and December 31, 2024:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
